# Map Tool > Prefetch and Prefetch WP Path: GMap.NET's TilePrefetcherMenu and TilePrefetcher over
# the planning screen (GCSViews/FlightPlanner.cs:5030-5080, 3305-3365).
#
# Prefetch: this map has no rubber-banded SelectedArea, so "No ripp area defined, ripp displayed on
# screen?" (Rip) comes every time; Yes takes the view. The menu offers a zoom range, 1 to 20 to
# begin with, refusing a minimum above the maximum, and counts the tiles per zoom with an estimate
# at 15,000 bytes a tile (TilePrefetcherMenu.cs:27-46). OK walks each zoom in turn; the form shows
# "Fetching tile at zoom (z): i of n, complete: p%" (TilePrefetcher.cs:200). Prefetch WP Path asks
# "max zoom" (20 offered) and walks every segment of the planned path at zooms 1 to that.
#
# Tiles offline: nothing is fetched, so a walk over an empty cache ends with nothing saved, which
# is what proves the walk ran to its end. The estimate's text is the menu's arithmetic.
#
# Needs no link: tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/plan-prefetch.gui

env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
setup mkdir -p "$WORK/MissionPlannerRust" && printf '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><Config><TXT_homelat>-35.3632621</TXT_homelat><TXT_homelng>149.1652374</TXT_homelng><TXT_homealt>584.1</TXT_homealt></Config>' > "$WORK/MissionPlannerRust/config.xml"
env MP_PLAN_DIR $WORK
tiles offline

screen plan
window 1600x1200
budget 23
expect mission.home true
expect plan.prefetch.state idle

# Prefetch: the question, the menu, the walk.
# The map first: a press before its first paint records nothing.
expect map.ready true
click map@0.45x0.40:right
click menu-mapTool
click menu-prefetch
expect plan.prompt Rip
expect plan.prompt.text No ripp area defined, ripp displayed on screen?
click plan-prompt-ok
expect plan.prompt none
expect plan.prefetch.menu 1-20
expect plan.prefetch.menu.total ~ Estimated:
expect plan.prefetch.menu.total ~ tiles for
# The maximum cannot go under the minimum, nor the minimum over the maximum.
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
expect plan.prefetch.menu 1-18
click plan-prefetch-min-up
click plan-prefetch-min-up
expect plan.prefetch.menu 3-18
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
click plan-prefetch-max-down
expect plan.prefetch.menu 3-3
# The C#'s size text ends with a space (sizeConverter), which a value here cannot carry.
expect plan.prefetch.menu.total ~ Estimated: 1 tile for 14.65 KB
click plan-prefetch-ok
expect plan.prefetch.walks 1
expect plan.prefetch.state done
expect plan.prefetch.ok 0
expect plan.prefetch.label ~ Fetching tile at zoom (3): 1 of 1, complete: 100%
click plan-prefetch-cancel
expect plan.prefetch.state idle

# No to the question leaves the map alone.
click map@0.45x0.40:right
click menu-mapTool
click menu-prefetch
click plan-prompt-cancel
expect plan.prompt none
expect plan.prefetch.menu none

# Prefetch WP Path: two waypoints make two segments from home; zooms 1 to 4 are eight walks.
click map@0.45x0.40
click map@0.60x0.55
expect mission.items 2
click map@0.30x0.70:right
click menu-mapTool
click menu-prefetchWPPath
expect plan.prompt max zoom
expect plan.prompt.text Enter the max zoom to prefetch to.
key ctrl+u
type 4
key Return
expect plan.prompt none
expect plan.prefetch.walks 8
expect plan.prefetch.state done
expect plan.prefetch.ok 0
click plan-prefetch-cancel

# A word for the zoom is "Invalid number entered".
click map@0.30x0.70:right
click menu-mapTool
click menu-prefetchWPPath
key ctrl+u
type lots
key Return
expect plan.prompt Error
expect plan.prompt.text Invalid number entered
click plan-prompt-ok
expect plan.prefetch.state idle
